{"round": 26, "actions": [1.99, 1.47], "thoughts": ["", "The data shows two consistent pricing strategies after round 25 under the new manager:\n\n- Price at 2.0 yields quantity sold about 33 and profit around 33.\n- Price at 1.47 yields quantity sold about 80 and profit around 37-38.\n\nProfit is (price - 1) * quantity. At 2.0, profit per unit is 1, selling ~33 units for profit ~33. At 1.47, profit per unit is 0.47, selling ~80 units for profit ~37.75.\n\nClearly, the lower price of 1.47 yields higher profit than 2.0. Also, the competitor is close to 2.0, which suggests there is a price segmentation or customers accepting different prices.\n\nThe previous manager also had high consistency of profit ~33 at 2.0 price, and ~38 at ~1.47 price points with high quantity sold at 1.47.\n\nMaximizing profit long term is best at price 1.47. Pricing at or near 1.47 increases quantity sold enough to offset per unit margin loss."], "respones": ["", "The data shows two consistent pricing strategies after round 25 under the new manager:\n\n- Price at 2.0 yields quantity sold about 33 and profit around 33.\n- Price at 1.47 yields quantity sold about 80 and profit around 37-38.\n\nProfit is (price - 1) * quantity. At 2.0, profit per unit is 1, selling ~33 units for profit ~33. At 1.47, profit per unit is 0.47, selling ~80 units for profit ~37.75.\n\nClearly, the lower price of 1.47 yields higher profit than 2.0. Also, the competitor is close to 2.0, which suggests there is a price segmentation or customers accepting different prices.\n\nThe previous manager also had high consistency of profit ~33 at 2.0 price, and ~38 at ~1.47 price points with high quantity sold at 1.47.\n\nMaximizing profit long term is best at price 1.47. Pricing at or near 1.47 increases quantity sold enough to offset per unit margin loss.\n\nMy chosen price: 1.47"], "demands": [10.034862765539138, 80.32374706598797], "profits": [9.934514137883747, 37.752161121014346], "gains": [-1.0787135134710555, 1.349422347